<article class="env-remark" id="0DJL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DJL">Remark <span data-tag="0DJL">36.18.3</span> <span class="named">(Variant with support)</span>.</a>  Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let $T \subset X$ be a closed subset such that $X \setminus T$ is quasi-compact. The analogue of Theorem <a href="/tag/09M5" data-tag="09M5">36.18.2</a> holds for $D_{\mathit{QCoh}, T}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. This follows from the exact same argument as in the proof of the theorem, using Lemmas <a href="/tag/0A9A" data-tag="0A9A">36.15.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0A9B" data-tag="0A9B">36.17.3</a> and a variant of Lemma <a href="/tag/09M3" data-tag="09M3">36.18.1</a> with supports. If we ever need this, we will precisely state the result here and give a detailed proof. </p>
</article>